# Composition → Design-Spec Sync

Apply when creating or modifying **group + item** component APIs in Storybook or framework ports.

## When this rule applies

- New files under `storybook-angular/src/components/ids-*-group/` or `*-group.component.ts`
- Splitting a monolithic component into `*-group` + item selectors
- Adding `IDS_*_IMPORTS` arrays that include both group and item components
- Changing `component-contracts/**/<slug>.contract.ts` to document group defaults or deprecate `options[]`

## Required actions (same PR / session)

1. Open `components/<programme>/<slug>/design-spec.md` (resolve programme from `config/design_systems/`).
2. Update **Anatomy**, **Composition & API (runtime)**, **Codegen Contract → Deterministic structure**, **Source Mapping**, and **Implementation Notes** as needed.
3. Follow the checklist in `.cursor/rules/design-spec-and-lit-workflow.mdc` → **Composition Pattern Sync**.
4. Use **design-spec-blueprint** skill for section wording and production-ready gate.

## Canonical pattern (document in spec)

```
Group [group-level props]
  Item [item-level props]
  Item …
```

Examples:
- `ids-checkbox-group` → `ids-checkbox`
- `ids-radio-button-group` → `ids-radio-button`
- `ids-accordion` → `ids-accordion-item` (+ header/body children)

**Synapse (IDS-fork):** inherit composition from `components/ids/<slug>/design-spec.md`; update `components/synapse/<slug>/design-spec.md` **Composition & API** and **Deterministic structure** in the same change (see `docs/design-spec-authoring-contract.md` → **Synapse (IDS-fork)**). **Storybook:** React only — no `storybook-angular/` Synapse ports unless explicitly requested.

## Do not

- Ship Storybook stories that use composition markup without updating the spec.
- Leave aggregate `options[]` / `items[]` as the only documented API when composition is preferred.
- Skip `component-contracts` updates when spec references a contract mirror path.
